From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 20:36:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 125/274] TileLang V4.1 WO: WO-A hands WO-B the reference's
 MXFP8 cast directly

WO-A wrote a BF16 a that per_token_cast read back and quantized: two extra trips
through memory (about 10 MB per 1024-row sequence-parallel slice) and two
kernels. WO-A's last kernel now rounds to BF16 and applies the same cast itself:
the in-kernel GEMM in its epilogue (fp8w_bf16_gemm_cast), the split decode path
in its reduce (splitk_reduce_cast). The bytes equal per_token_cast of the BF16 a
(test_wo_a_casts_as_per_token_cast), so WO's output is unchanged. WO-B runs its
GEMM on them (_block32_gemm); everything live is borrowed in one carve.

